  # TestEveryFleetRouteRefusesATenantKey is Faz A.1 Task 3, and it needs its OWN alternative for the same
  # reason: none of the words already on this line is a substring of it, so without one this test would ride
  # `make test-component` reporting nothing at all — this repository's signature failure. It reads its route
  # list off apps/control-plane/api/router.go's OWN source (never a pasted list) and drives EVERY runner /
  # runner-pool / runner-pool-key route the shipped router registers, over a real Postgres with the REAL
  # fleet.RegistryAPI mounted: a tenant key is refused on every one, and a system-scoped key (carrying
  # `provision` and `approve` too, so the ONLY thing standing between it and a route is systemOnly) is not.
  if test "$status" -eq 0; then
